default GBA carts to gpSP

This changes behaviour rather than making upstream work here, and is
here because the default is a performance question on this hardware.

slot picks mGBA for every platform unless Config/selected_core.txt
names a core for that cart, and the only way to name one is the START
core picker, one game at a time. On the Mini Flip's Cortex-A7 mGBA
interprets GBA code and takes 14-18 ms a frame against a 16.7 ms
budget, so a cart nobody has picked a core for plays at roughly half
speed. gpSP has an ARM dynarec and takes 6.3 ms. An unconfigured GBA
cart should start on the core that can play it.

Game Boy and Game Boy Color stay on mGBA; gpSP only runs GBA. A line in
selected_core.txt still wins, so a cart gpSP gets wrong can be moved
back to mGBA in the picker.

core_for takes no platform and its one caller is the GBA-only picker,
so it falls back to the GBA default rather than to Core::default,
which stays mGBA as the initial value of an app with nothing seated.

Resume and quick-save states are kept per core, so a GBA cart that was
last played on mGBA by default will not find its old states under
gpSP. Battery saves (.sav) are shared and carry over.

Tests that assumed a GBA cart starts on mGBA are updated: the core-picker
tests pin their carts to mGBA, the unconfigured-default test asserts
gpSP, and the e2e and play tests look for resume states under gpSP.

